From ab85fe895ba3968f828ffe2759d931b045497a93 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 17:21:39 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 52/52] Test text placement in KiCad schematic SVG exports
 against KiCad's

KiCad's command line tests come with KiCad's own SVG export of a
schematic, qa/data/cli/basic_test, in which KiCad marks every text it
draws. Every text gerbonara draws has to be within a small tolerance of
where KiCad draws it, and every text KiCad draws around the schematic's
contents has to be drawn. This checks the placement, rotation and
alignment of symbol fields (including those of rotated and mirrored
symbols), pin names and numbers, labels, free text and text boxes.

KiCad 9.0.6 and KiCad 10 come with different exports of the same
schematic, so it is checked against both. Copies that are the same in
several KiCad versions are only tested once.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_013wvKon1yvwjNtAdtSuZzZh
